## Key Concepts

### 1. DB Instance
- A self-contained database environment running on dedicated compute resources
- Contains multiple user databases
- Can be accessed via JDBC, ODBC, or database-specific connection methods

### 2. DB Subnet Group
- Collection of subnets designated for RDS database
- Must span at least 2 AZs for Multi-AZ deployments
- Required for VPC deployments

### 3. Security Groups
- Control inbound/outbound traffic to RDS instance
- Default port: 3306 (MySQL), 5432 (PostgreSQL), 1433 (SQL Server), 5984 (Oracle)

### 4. Parameter Groups
- Define database engine configuration parameters
- Can be modified without restarting DB instance (some parameters)

### 5. Option Groups
- Provide additional features and functionality
- Examples: S3 integration, enhanced monitoring, timezone support

### 6. Automated Backups
- Automatic daily backup retention (1-35 days)
- Transaction logs backed up every 5 minutes
- Enable point-in-time recovery (PITR)

### 7. DB Snapshots
- Manual snapshots created on-demand
- Persist indefinitely until manually deleted
- Can be copied to different regions

### 8. Multi-AZ Deployment
- Primary database in one AZ
- Standby replica in another AZ
- Synchronous replication
- Automatic failover on primary failure

### 9. Read Replicas
- Asynchronous replication of primary database
- Can be in same region or different regions
- Scale read operations independently
- Promote to standalone DB if needed

