## Deployment Options

### 1. Single-AZ Deployment
- Database in single availability zone
- Lower cost
- No automatic failover on failure
- Good for: Development, testing, non-critical workloads

```bash
# Create Single-AZ instance
aws rds create-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier single-az-db \
  --multi-az false \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.micro
```

### 2. Multi-AZ Deployment
- Primary database in one AZ
- Standby replica in another AZ
- Synchronous replication
- Automatic failover (typically 1-2 minutes)
- 2x storage cost
- Good for: Production workloads, high availability

```bash
# Create Multi-AZ instance
aws rds create-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier multi-az-db \
  --multi-az true \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.small
```

### 3. Read Replicas
- Asynchronous replication
- Scale read operations
- Can be promoted to independent DB
- Can be in different regions (for DR)

```bash
# Create Read Replica (same region)
aws rds create-db-instance-read-replica \
  --db-instance-identifier mysql-prod-read-replica \
  --source-db-instance-identifier mysql-prod \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.small

# Create Read Replica (different region)
aws rds create-db-instance-read-replica \
  --db-instance-identifier mysql-prod-read-replica-us-west \
  --source-db-instance-identifier mysql-prod \
  --source-region us-east-1 \
  --region us-west-2 \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.small
```

