## Instance Types and Classes

### 1. General Purpose (db.t3, db.t4g) - Balanced
- **Best for:** Web applications, small to medium databases
- **Characteristics:** Burstable CPU, good performance/cost ratio
- **vCPU:** 1-16 cores
- **Memory:** 1 GB - 64 GB

```
db.t3.micro (1 vCPU, 1 GB RAM) - Free tier eligible
db.t3.small (2 vCPU, 2 GB RAM)
db.t3.medium (2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM)
db.t3.large (2 vCPU, 8 GB RAM)
```

### 2. Memory Optimized (db.r5, db.r6g) - High Performance
- **Best for:** Large databases, in-memory caching, data warehousing
- **Characteristics:** High memory-to-CPU ratio, sustained performance
- **vCPU:** 2-96 cores
- **Memory:** 16 GB - 768 GB

```
db.r5.large (2 vCPU, 16 GB RAM)
db.r5.xlarge (4 vCPU, 32 GB RAM)
db.r5.2xlarge (8 vCPU, 64 GB RAM)
db.r6g.xlarge (4 vCPU, 32 GB RAM) - Graviton2 processor
```

### 3. Compute Optimized (db.c5, db.c6g) - High CPU
- **Best for:** OLTP workloads, analytics queries
- **Characteristics:** High CPU-to-memory ratio
- **vCPU:** 1-72 cores

