## Step-by-Step Examples

### Example 1: Create MySQL RDS Instance

#### Step 1: Create DB Subnet Group

```bash
# Create DB Subnet Group (spans multiple AZs)
aws rds create-db-subnet-group \
  --db-subnet-group-name my-db-subnet \
  --db-subnet-group-description "Subnet group for RDS" \
  --subnet-ids subnet-12345678 subnet-87654321 \
  --tags Key=Name,Value=MyDBSubnet Key=Environment,Value=Production
```

#### Step 2: Create Security Group

```bash
# Create security group for RDS
aws ec2 create-security-group \
  --group-name rds-mysql-sg \
  --description "Security group for MySQL RDS" \
  --vpc-id vpc-12345678

# Get security group ID
RDS_SG=$(aws ec2 describe-security-groups \
  --filters Name=group-name,Values=rds-mysql-sg \
  --query 'SecurityGroups[0].GroupId' \
  --output text)

# Allow MySQL traffic (port 3306) from application servers
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
  --group-id $RDS_SG \
  --protocol tcp \
  --port 3306 \
  --source-security-group-id sg-app-servers

# Allow from EC2 instance CIDR (optional)
aws ec2 authorize-security-group-ingress \
  --group-id $RDS_SG \
  --protocol tcp \
  --port 3306 \
  --cidr 10.0.0.0/8
```

#### Step 3: Create RDS Instance

```bash
# Create MySQL RDS instance
aws rds create-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.small \
  --engine mysql \
  --engine-version 8.0.35 \
  --master-username admin \
  --master-user-password MySecurePassword123! \
  --allocated-storage 100 \
  --storage-type gp3 \
  --storage-iops 3000 \
  --storage-throughput 125 \
  --db-subnet-group-name my-db-subnet \
  --vpc-security-group-ids $RDS_SG \
  --multi-az true \
  --publicly-accessible false \
  --backup-retention-period 30 \
  --preferred-backup-window "03:00-04:00" \
  --preferred-maintenance-window "mon:04:00-mon:05:00" \
  --enable-cloudwatch-logs-exports error,general,slowquery \
  --tags Key=Name,Value=MyAppDB Key=Environment,Value=Production \
  --enable-iam-database-authentication \
  --deletion-protection
```

**Parameter Breakdown:**
- `--db-instance-class db.t3.small`: 2 vCPU, 2 GB RAM
- `--engine mysql`: MySQL database engine
- `--engine-version 8.0.35`: MySQL version 8.0.35
- `--allocated-storage 100`: Initial storage 100 GB
- `--storage-type gp3`: General Purpose SSD with IOPS
- `--storage-iops 3000`: 3,000 IOPS
- `--multi-az true`: High availability across AZs
- `--backup-retention-period 30`: 30-day backup retention
- `--enable-iam-database-authentication`: Use IAM for password-less authentication

#### Step 4: Monitor Creation

```bash
# Check status
aws rds describe-db-instances \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --query 'DBInstances[0].[DBInstanceStatus,AvailabilityZone,PendingModifiedValues]'

# Wait for available status (takes 5-10 minutes)
aws rds wait db-instance-available \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db

# Get endpoint
aws rds describe-db-instances \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --query 'DBInstances[0].Endpoint'
```

#### Step 5: Connect to Database

```bash
# From EC2 instance in same VPC
mysql -h myapp-db.c9akciq32.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com \
       -u admin \
       -p

# Enter password when prompted
# Enter password: MySecurePassword123!

# Create database
mysql> CREATE DATABASE myapp;
mysql> USE myapp;
mysql> CREATE TABLE users (
  id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
  name VARCHAR(100),
  email VARCHAR(100),
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

# Verify
mysql> SHOW TABLES;
mysql> DESCRIBE users;
```

