### Example 2: Create PostgreSQL Read Replica

```bash
# Create Read Replica for scaling reads
aws rds create-db-instance-read-replica \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db-read \
  --source-db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.small \
  --publicly-accessible false

# Wait for replica to be available
aws rds wait db-instance-available \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db-read

# Connect to read replica (read-only)
psql -h myapp-db-read.c9akciq32.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com \
     -U postgres \
     -d myapp

# Queries work, writes fail on replica
postgres=> SELECT * FROM users;
postgres=> INSERT INTO users VALUES (1, 'John', 'john@example.com');
ERROR: cannot execute INSERT in a read-only transaction
```

