## Backup and Recovery

### Automated Backups

```bash
# Enable automated backups (default)
aws rds modify-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --backup-retention-period 30 \
  --preferred-backup-window "03:00-04:00" \
  --copy-tags-to-snapshot

# Backups include:
# - Daily full backup
# - Transaction logs every 5 minutes
# - Enables point-in-time recovery (PITR)

# Restore to specific point in time
aws rds restore-db-instance-to-point-in-time \
  --source-db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --target-db-instance-identifier myapp-db-restored-pit \
  --restore-time 2025-11-25T15:30:00Z

# Automatic backups retained for 1-35 days
```

### Manual Snapshots

```bash
# Create snapshot
aws rds create-db-snapshot \
  --db-snapshot-identifier myapp-db-backup-manual-20251125 \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db

# List snapshots
aws rds describe-db-snapshots \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db

# Copy snapshot to different region (DR)
aws rds copy-db-snapshot \
  --source-db-snapshot-identifier myapp-db-backup-manual-20251125 \
  --target-db-snapshot-identifier myapp-db-backup-us-west-2 \
  --source-region us-east-1 \
  --region us-west-2

# Delete old snapshots
aws rds delete-db-snapshot \
  --db-snapshot-identifier myapp-db-backup-manual-20251125
```

