## High Availability and Disaster Recovery

### Multi-AZ Deployment

```bash
# Enable Multi-AZ (synchronous replication)
aws rds modify-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --multi-az true \
  --apply-immediately

# Automatic failover on:
# - Hardware failure
# - Availability Zone failure
# - Network failure
# - Database process crash
# - Storage failure

# Failover time: Typically 1-2 minutes
# Connection strings automatically updated

# Manual failover (for testing)
aws rds reboot-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --force-failover
```

### Read Replicas for Disaster Recovery

```bash
# Create cross-region read replica (disaster recovery)
aws rds create-db-instance-read-replica \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db-dr \
  --source-db-instance-identifier myapp-db \
  --source-region us-east-1 \
  --region us-west-2 \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.small

# In case of primary region failure, promote replica to standalone
aws rds promote-read-replica \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-db-dr \
  --backup-retention-period 7

# Now myapp-db-dr is independent database accepting writes
```

