## Real-World Use Cases

### Use Case 1: E-Commerce Platform

**Scenario:** Multi-tier application with varying read/write patterns

```bash
# Primary database (writes)
aws rds create-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier ecommerce-primary \
  --db-instance-class db.r5.xlarge \
  --engine mysql \
  --multi-az true \
  --allocated-storage 500 \
  --iops 5000

# Read replicas for scaling reads
aws rds create-db-instance-read-replica \
  --db-instance-identifier ecommerce-read-1 \
  --source-db-instance-identifier ecommerce-primary \
  --db-instance-class db.r5.large

aws rds create-db-instance-read-replica \
  --db-instance-identifier ecommerce-read-2 \
  --source-db-instance-identifier ecommerce-primary \
  --db-instance-class db.r5.large

# Application routing:
# - Product catalog queries → Read replicas
# - Order writes → Primary database
# - User writes → Primary database
# - Analytics queries → Read replicas
```

**Benefits:**
- High availability with Multi-AZ
- Scale reads independently
- Reduced load on primary

### Use Case 2: SaaS Multi-Tenant Application

**Scenario:** Each tenant has isolated database

```bash
# Create tenant database
create_tenant_db() {
  TENANT_ID=$1
  aws rds create-db-instance \
    --db-instance-identifier saas-tenant-$TENANT_ID \
    --db-instance-class db.t3.small \
    --engine postgres \
    --allocated-storage 50 \
    --backup-retention-period 7
}

# Create databases for multiple tenants
for i in {1..100}; do
  create_tenant_db $i &
done
wait

# Benefits:
# - Data isolation per tenant
# - Independent scaling
# - Easy billing per tenant
# - Simplified backup/recovery per tenant
```

### Use Case 3: Data Warehouse / Analytics

```bash
# Large instance for analytical workloads
aws rds create-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier analytics-db \
  --db-instance-class db.r5.4xlarge \
  --engine postgres \
  --allocated-storage 2000 \
  --storage-type gp3 \
  --iops 20000

# Read replicas for concurrent queries
aws rds create-db-instance-read-replica \
  --db-instance-identifier analytics-read-1 \
  --source-db-instance-identifier analytics-db \
  --db-instance-class db.r5.2xlarge

# Benefits:
# - High memory for complex queries
# - IOPS for concurrent access
# - Read replicas for parallel queries
```

### Use Case 4: Development/Test/Production Environments

```bash
# Production - Multi-AZ with backups
aws rds create-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-prod \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.medium \
  --multi-az true \
  --backup-retention-period 30

# Staging - Restored from production snapshot
aws rds restore-db-instance-from-db-snapshot \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-staging \
  --db-snapshot-identifier myapp-prod-snapshot-latest \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.small

# Development - Smallest instance
aws rds create-db-instance \
  --db-instance-identifier myapp-dev \
  --db-instance-class db.t3.micro \
  --backup-retention-period 1
```

